  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the converse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** $4$ is even, **then** $5$ is odd.",
  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ $4$ is even.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $5$ is odd.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $5$ is odd, then $4$ is even.",
